# Ultra-Gaming OS (Custom Resolution Edition)

High-performance system configuration with **Manual Resolution Control**.
Optimized for PC, Laptop, and Tablet environments at 165Hz.

## Features
- **Display Control**: Manual resolution switching via command-line or UI.
- **Refresh Rate**: Forced 165Hz for maximum fluidity.
- **Kernel**: Low-latency Gaming Kernel.
- **UI**: Aero Glass with Custom Branding and High-Contrast Cursor.
- **Audio**: Hardware Startup Chime & Legacy Shutdown SFX.

## Pre-installed Games
- HoK, PGR, Genshin, Honkai, Space Pinball.
#!/bin/bash
# Deployment Script with Custom Resolution Support
# Targeted for Desktop & Tablet

set -e

# --- Visual & Branding ---
sudo cp ./assets/branding_logo.svg /usr/share/plasma/look-and-feel/aero/contents/images/start.svg
kwriteconfig6 --group "Mouse" --key "cursorTheme" "Enhanced_White"
kwriteconfig6 --group "Mouse" --key "cursorSize" 48

# --- Display & Refresh Rate (Force 165Hz) ---
kwriteconfig6 --file kwinrc --group "Compositing" --key "MaxFPS" 165
kwriteconfig6 --file kwinrc --group "Compositing" --key "RefreshRate" 165

# --- [ NEW: RESOLUTION CUSTOMIZER ] ---
# Creating a tool to manually set resolution
sudo cat <<EOF > /usr/local/bin/set-res
#!/bin/bash
# Usage: set-res 1920 1080
if [ -z "\$1" ] || [ -z "\$2" ]; then
    echo "Usage: set-res [width] [height]"
    exit 1
fi
# Apply resolution and force 165Hz
wlr-randr --output \$(wlr-randr | grep -oP '^[A-Za-z0-9-]+') --mode "\$1x\$2@165" || xrandr --size "\$1x\$2" --rate 165
echo "Resolution set to \$1x\$2 at 165Hz"
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/set-res

# --- Audio Integration ---
sudo cp ./assets/boot_chime.wav /usr/share/sounds/
sudo cp ./assets/exit_sound.wav /usr/share/sounds/
echo "aplay /usr/share/sounds/boot_chime.wav &" >> ~/.config/autostart-scripts/boot.sh
echo "alias shutdown='aplay /usr/share/sounds/exit_sound.wav && poweroff'" >> ~/.bashrc

# --- Optimization Engine ---
sudo cat <<EOF > /usr/local/bin/sys-opt
#!/bin/bash
echo "performance" | sudo tee /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/scaling_governor
echo 3 | sudo tee /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches
notify-send "SYSTEM" "PERFORMANCE MODE ACTIVE"
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/sys-opt

echo "INSTALLATION COMPLETE. Use 'set-res width height' to customize resolution."
